Input: {"question": "When was the Dallas County Courthouse built?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d00", "start": 0, "end": 108, "text": "Dallas County Courthouse (Iowa) The Dallas County Courthouse in Adel, Iowa, United States was built in 1902."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d00", "start": 109, "end": 255, "text": "It was individually listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1973, and is a part of the County Courthouses in Iowa Thematic Resource."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d00", "start": 256, "end": 351, "text": "In 2009 it was included as a contributing property in the Adel Public Square Historic District."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d00", "start": 352, "end": 448, "text": "The current structure is the fourth building to house court functions and county administration."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d00", "start": 449, "end": 573, "text": "Dallas County's first courthouse was a double log cabin constructed of cottonwood logs and served the county from 1848-1853."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d00", "start": 574, "end": 631, "text": "County leaders constructed a second courthouse that was a"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d01", "start": 0, "end": 11, "text": "Market No ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d01", "start": 12, "end": 114, "text": "1 Addition Downtown Perry Historic District Jones Business College Perry Carnegie Library Building St."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0006-177e55560693:d01", "start": 115, "end": 228, "text": "Patrick 's Catholic Church Redfield Redfield GAR Hall Van Meter Robert William Andrew Feller Farmstead Waukee St."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs